# Gaston project conventions

Kotlin Multiplatform fuel & EV station finder — `:shared` (models, networking, providers) and `:androidApp` (Compose phone UI + Car App Library for Android Auto).

## Build & verify

```bash
./gradlew :androidApp:assembleFullDebug          # local debug APK
./gradlew --no-daemon :androidApp:assembleDebug :androidApp:lintFullDebug :shared:build   # CI-equivalent
./gradlew :shared:testAndroidHostTest            # shared unit tests on JVM
```

- JDK 17+, Android Studio Koala+
- Secrets in `local.properties` only (never commit keys). See `docs/ENV_VARS.md`, `docs/API_KEYS.md`
- New POI/country providers: follow existing `*Provider` / `*Client` patterns under `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/fr/geoking/gaston/api/`

## Code style

- Match surrounding Kotlin: explicit types when clarity helps, avoid drive-by refactors
- Phone UI: Jetpack Compose + Material 3 in `androidApp/.../ui/`
- Android Auto: Car App Library templates in `androidApp/.../auto/` — keep templates safe and minimal while driving
- Networking: Ktor in `:shared`; DI via Koin
- Persistence: Room in `:androidApp` for on-device cache/history
- Prefer extending an existing provider/client over new parallel abstractions

## Scope reminders

- Do not add Play Billing, Firebase, or new data sources unless requested
- Provider API keys are optional toggles — do not hardcode secrets
- 16 KB page size: no new native code; CI runs `lintFullDebug` for alignment issues
